# Files generated by `rust/imas_rs/imas_updater/build_ids.py`.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` tells GitHub two things: collapse the file by default in pull
# request diffs, and leave it out of the repository language statistics. The files stay
# tracked, stay diffable, and can still be expanded and reviewed in a pull request; this
# only changes how GitHub presents them by default. It has no effect on `git diff` locally.
#
# It matters here because the generated code is larger than the hand-written code, so
# without this a regeneration buries the real changes in a pull request, and the language
# breakdown describes the IMAS Data Dictionary rather than GSFit.
#
# Never hand-edit these; regenerate instead. See `rust/imas_rs/imas_updater/README.md`.

# One Rust file per IDS. Listed rather than globbed, because `src/ids/mod.rs` sits beside
# them and is hand-maintained (it carries a `pub mod` line per IDS). Adding an IDS means
# adding a line here too.
rust/imas_rs/src/ids/core_profiles.rs             linguist-generated=true
rust/imas_rs/src/ids/core_sources.rs              linguist-generated=true
